# Internationalization (i18n)

Uses Flutter's official ARB + `flutter gen-l10n`. No external packages.

## Files

- `lib/i18n/app_en.arb` — Template (source of truth)
- `lib/i18n/app_pt.arb` — Portuguese translations
- `lib/i18n/generated/` — Auto-generated (NEVER edit manually)

## After editing ARB files

Run `flutter gen-l10n` to regenerate `AppLocalizations`.

## Accessing translations

Always use the extension, never `AppLocalizations.of(context)!` directly:

```dart
import '../../core/extensions/build_context_extensions.dart';

// In any widget:
final t = context.translate;
Text(t.settingsTitle);
```

## ARB key naming convention

Keys follow `featureContext` pattern:

```
navHome              → nav feature, home label
settingsDarkTheme    → settings feature, dark theme
launchesTitle        → launches feature, page title
errorNoConnection    → error (global), no connection
```

## Rules

- **presentation/pages and widgets** → use `context.translate`
- **domain and data layers** → NEVER import i18n (pure Dart)
- **No hardcoded user-facing strings** in widgets — always use ARB keys
- **English ARB is the template** — every key must exist in `app_en.arb` first
- **Portuguese ARB must have all keys** from the English template
